From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sinful1992 <sinful1992@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 00:57:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Batch the reads GetMediaSources repeats per item across a
 page of DTOs

Building a page of DTOs calls item.GetMediaSources() per item, and that
reads media streams, attachments, alternate-version links (twice) and
the media-segment flag from the database: five round-trips per item,
buried in BaseItem.GetVersionInfo where a batch cannot be passed in. EF
logging on a 134-episode series list with the Android TV app's field
set: ~1,400 commands, ~1 s, of which the database itself was under
100 ms. The cost is round-trips, not data.

PagePrefetch (Jellyfin.Server.Implementations) is a request-scoped,
AsyncLocal batch of those reads. DtoService opens it for a page, loading
each batch through the concrete repositories in one query apiece, and
the readers -- MediaSourceManager for streams and attachments,
LibraryManager for alternate-version ids, MediaSegmentManager for the
segment flag -- answer whole-item reads from it while it is open. It is
gone when the method returns, so nothing is cached across requests and
there is no staleness window. A covered item the batch did not return
reads as empty; an item outside the scope falls through as before.

MediaBrowser.Controller, the assembly plugins bind against, is not
touched: the loaders sit on the concrete classes and are reached by type
test, and the readers already live in assemblies this fork replaces.
